`sortedImportPaths` duplicates `sortedStringsMapKeys` one-for-one — `sortedImportPaths(imports)` is exactly `sortedStringsMapKeys[bool](imports)` since `map[string]bool` is the only concrete type it's ever called with. Three call sites use this one (`pin.go:126`, `pin.go:227`, `pin.go:671`), two use the generic (`pin.go:743`, `pin.go:950`).

```suggestion
func sortedImportPaths(imports map[string]bool) []string {
	return sortedStringsMapKeys(imports)
}
```

Or, to remove the duplication entirely rather than just delegate, replace the three `sortedImportPaths(...)` call sites with `sortedStringsMapKeys(...)` and delete this function.

